<http://data.silknow.org/object/63d1bbb5-ec9c-3382-b658-5d7b1ecc013a>
        a                              ecrm:E22_Man-Made_Object ;
        rdfs:comment                   "Imperial robe, silk tapestry (<i>kesi</i>) with painted details, China, Qing dynasty, probably early 18th century"@en , "Imperial Robe of silk tapestry (<i>kesi</i>), woven in coloured silks and gold thread on a purple-grey ground. Some of the details have been executed with the brush.\nThe design is composed of eight circular medallions, each containing a pair of five-clawed dragons in the midst of scrolled clouds upon a fretted background shaped in the centre into a <i>shou</i> (longevity) character. The border and sleeves are mounted with a brocade of similar design on a dark ground."@en ;
        ecrm:P138i_has_representation  <http://data.silknow.org/image/c42cb6d7-aacd-3e28-880a-4fcddbbb799b> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note               "Imperial robe, silk tapestry (<i>kesi</i>) with painted details, China, Qing dynasty, probably early 18th century"@en , "Imperial Robe of silk tapestry (<i>kesi</i>), woven in coloured silks and gold thread on a purple-grey ground. Some of the details have been executed with the brush.\nThe design is composed of eight circular medallions, each containing a pair of five-clawed dragons in the midst of scrolled clouds upon a fretted background shaped in the centre into a <i>shou</i> (longevity) character. The border and sleeves are mounted with a brocade of similar design on a dark ground."@en ;
